@startuml CodexTopology
!includeurl https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/refs/heads/main/proveo.iuml
' purpose: the codex def's resolved topology — the harness layer, the seeded $CODEX_HOME, the loop, and the container boundary
' covers: defs/codex/**
' covers: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh
' covers: internal/contract/image_size_test.go
'   how the harness is steered and gated _spec/defs/codex/codex-paradigm.puml
'   the empty-apt guard ................ _spec/defs/harness-image-layers.puml
'
' ── CONFIG.TOML: THE KIT WRITES, PROVEO MERGES (2026-10-24, user: "Delete dup
' keys, merge the rest") ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' MEASURED: on sbx, seed_codex_defaults never ran — proveo_sbx_passthrough
' exec'd past it (v2), and v3 launches the codex kit's ENTRYPOINT, not
' /entrypoint.sh. The kit's install hook rewrites config.toml on every create
' (approval_policy, sandbox_mode, mcp_oauth_credentials_store, and per auth mode
' forced_login_method + [model_providers.sandboxd]). So:
'   * approval_policy and sandbox_mode left defs/codex/defaults/config.toml;
'     the non-sbx path still launches with --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-
'     sandbox (entrypoint.sh), so nothing relied on the keys.
'   * proveo_merge_codex_defaults (entrypoint-lib.sh) inserts each missing
'     top-level default ABOVE the file's first [table] (below it, TOML would
'     read the key as the table's); CODEX_RESEED=1 resets those keys only. It
'     runs in proveo_seed after proveo_sync_config restore, and replaced
'     seed_codex_defaults's whole-file copy.
'   Pinned by internal/contract/codex_defaults_merge_test.go.
'
' ── NO DOCKER BINARIES OF ITS OWN (N14, DONE (wt) 2026-10-17) ──────────────
' codex was the one harness image Cut 4 missed: its Dockerfile still installed
' docker-29.7.2's static tarball and symlinked dockerd, shadowing the Engine
' proveo/base inherits from the sbx template. codex was absent from
' image_size_test.go harnessDockerfiles, so TestNoHarnessImageShipsDockerBinaries
' never read it. The user: "Delete the layer (Recommended)". MEASURED: the RUN
' is gone from defs/codex/Dockerfile, codex heads harnessDockerfiles
' (image_size_test.go:173-174), and the test was red before, green after
' (reported). The group, the start-docker LABEL (Dockerfile:47-50 since N26)
' and iptables stay — _spec/_devops/image-size-reduction.puml, Cut 4.
'
' ── NO APT LAYER OF ITS OWN (N26, DONE (wt) 2026-10-18) ────────────────────
' The image installs nothing through apt. Its apt RUN named no package: it
' paid an `apt-get update` and two cache mounts (proveo-codex-apt-cache,
' proveo-codex-apt-lists) for nothing, then ran `proveo-harden /usr /opt`.
' MEASURED: the RUN is deleted, and the file calls proveo-harden nowhere.
' base-node-lsp already runs that pass over /usr /opt, and only user and group
' edits sit between FROM and where the layer was (Dockerfile:13-41).
' internal/contract TestEveryAptInstallNamesAPackage now fails any tracked
' Dockerfile whose `apt-get install` names no package; it found opencode's twin.
' Image (MEASURED by the coordinator): rebuilt with the cache off, `docker
' history` shows no apt layer, and TestImageCodex passes.
' defs/codex/README.md's variants table now lists proveo/codex as the base of
' proveo/codex-browser; TestBrowserVariantsAreDocumentedAsALayerOnTheirHarness
' (internal/contract/browser_layer_test.go) refuses the old claim in any README.
'
' ── AUTH: THE LOGIN FILE IS A CREDENTIAL (moved from source, N14) ──────────
' Two ways in: a ChatGPT-plan login at $CODEX_HOME/auth.json, which the durable
' proveo home carries between runs, or OPENAI_API_KEY. With both present the
' login wins — codex's own default — and proveo withholds the competing key
' host-side for the same reason (_spec/internal/credentials/
' credential-decisions.puml: a login on disk out-ranks an env token).
' So the .codex home mount declares NO deny list — claudecode's posture, not
' cursor's. `codex login` writes ~/.codex/auth.json and a ChatGPT-plan run IS
' that file. Scrubbing it would make every subscription session log in again,
' and would hide the login from PersistedLogin, which is what stops proveo
' injecting a competing API key.
'
' ── codex-browser ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' defs/base-node-browser/Dockerfile applied onto proveo/codex (browserOf in
' internal/imagebuild/targets.go; _spec/defs/browser-layer.puml), so it is a
' strict superset: the language servers the entrypoint wires in as MCP servers
' are still there. Selected per run as the `browser` addon, never as a target
' of its own. (The manifest comment said FROM proveo/base-node-browser; that
' predates the layer-on-harness inversion and was not carried over.)
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam ranksep 120
skinparam nodesep 80

left to right direction

title Codex CLI Topology — ML Blackbox Loop

actor "Human" as Human
actor "Codex CLI\n(codex)" as Codex

package "Harness Layer" as Harness {
 component "entrypoint.sh\n(docker)" as Entrypoint <<script>>
 component ".env loader\nOPENAI_API_KEY / auth.json check" as EnvLoader <<logic>>
 component "smoke-test mode" as Smoke <<mode>>
 component "steering detection\nAGENTS.md (native) | CLAUDE.md (fallback)" as Steering <<prompt>>
 component "verification discovery\nbuild / test / lint" as Verify0 <<logic>>
}

package "User Layer — $CODEX_HOME" as Home {
 component "config.toml\nkit: approval · sandbox · login · provider\nproveo: hide_agent_reasoning · doc fallbacks" as Config <<config>>
 component "AGENTS.md\nproveo house rules" as HouseRules <<prompt>>
 component "agents/*.toml\nread-only advisors\n+ spec-keeper (workspace-write)" as Subagents <<subagent>>
 component "[mcp_servers.lsp_*]\nmcp-language-server" as LspMcp <<logic>>
 database "sessions/**.jsonl\nrollouts — what `resume` reads" as Sessions <<db>>
 component "auth.json\n`codex login`" as Auth <<security>>
}

package "Execution Loop" as Loop {
 component "Spec / Goal" as Spec <<step>>
 component "Plan + Acceptance Criteria" as Plan <<step>>
 component "Implement (edit)" as Implement <<step>>
 component "Verify (run tests/lint)" as Verify <<step>>
 component "Inspect Failure → Adjust" as Inspect <<step>>
}

package "Container Sandbox" as Sandbox {
 component "codex --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox\n(the container is the sandbox)" as Force <<flag>>
 component "/app workspace mount\nruns as host uid (non-root)" as Mounts <<storage>>
 component "network egress layer\nopen | allowlist | review" as Net <<security>>
}

cloud "OpenAI backend\napi.openai.com" as Backend

Human --> Entrypoint : starts container
Entrypoint --> EnvLoader
Entrypoint --> Smoke
Entrypoint --> Steering : report, never write
Entrypoint --> Verify0
Entrypoint --> Home : proveo_seed codex\n(merge missing keys)
Entrypoint --> Codex : " exec ""codex --dangerously-bypass-…"" "
Codex --> Config
Codex --> HouseRules
Codex --> Steering : reads project AGENTS.md
Codex --> Subagents : in-loop review gates
Codex --> LspMcp : code intelligence over MCP
Codex --> Sessions : writes each turn
Codex --> Loop : executes loop
Loop --> Verify : runs detected commands
Verify -> Inspect : on failure
Inspect -> Plan : next iteration
Force --> Sandbox : within\ncontainer boundary
Codex -[#00BAC6,dashed,bold]-> Backend : inference
Auth ..> Backend : login OR OPENAI_API_KEY
Net ..> Backend : provider pin = "".openai.com""

note right of Home
  **$CODEX_HOME is $HOME/.codex, and $HOME is what proveo redirects.**
  The manifest mounts the durable ""~/.proveo/.codex"" at
  ""/proveo-home/.codex"" and sets ""HOME=/proveo-home"", so config,
  house rules, composed subagents, the login and every session
  transcript outlive ""--rm"".

  This is why ""CODEX_HOME"" is deliberately NOT baked into the image.
  An absolute path frozen at build time resolves past the mount, back
  into the image's own home — and everything above is silently
  discarded with the container. The entrypoint resolves it ONCE and
  exports it, so the CLI and every helper agree.
end note

note as CodexHomeSeed #F4F9FB
  **It resolves from the SEED's home, not from ""$HOME"" directly, and
  the two are not always the same one.** ""proveo_seed"" finds its
  destination through ""_proveo_agent_home"", which prefers
  ""PROVEO_HOME"" — while under sbx a setup command runs as user "1000",
  which resets ""HOME"" from ""/etc/passwd"".

  A ""CODEX_HOME"" taken from the process's own ""HOME"" can therefore name
  a directory the seed never wrote to, holding none of the config,
  house rules or subagents just installed. That surfaces as a session
  coming up with no setup and no error to explain it, which is
  why the entrypoint warns when an inherited value disagrees.
end note

note bottom of Subagents
  **codex declares agents as TOML documents, not markdown with
  frontmatter**, so the shared body arrives as a
  ""developer_instructions"" VALUE — composed at start by
  ""render_subagents"", from one body per agent plus codex's own
  frontmatter. Same bodies as every other harness; different container.

  The value is a multi-line LITERAL string, never a basic one: literal
  strings process no escapes, and the bodies document backslash
  sequences on purpose. A basic string would eat them with no error,
  in a file nobody re-reads after composing it.
end note

note bottom of Sandbox
  **Codex's own sandbox is off by default, and the reason is NOT
  cursor's.** Landlock+seccomp needs no unprivileged userns, so it
  can actually engage in this cap-dropped container. It is off
  because confining the agent to part of a tree that is already a
  disposable copy buys little, while its approval prompts are fatal
  to an unattended run — a stall with nobody to answer.

  ""PROVEO_CODEX_SANDBOX"" turns it back on as
  ""--sandbox <mode> --ask-for-approval never"".

  The posture is written in BOTH places on purpose: on the argv, and
  in the seeded ""config.toml"". The config half is what makes
  ""codex exec"", ""codex resume"" and a bare ""codex"" agree without
  depending on where a flag lands in the argv.
end note

note right of LspMcp
  **LSP arrives over MCP because codex has no external-LSP config** —
  the same bridge cursor uses. The block is written into
  ""config.toml"" between ""# >>> proveo lsp"" markers, so an operator's
  own ""[mcp_servers.*]"" entries survive a re-run and only what proveo
  generated is replaced.

  It is APPENDED, and TOML requires top-level keys to precede every
  table: a key added below the marker would be read as belonging to
  the last generated table. Operators add theirs above it.
end note

@enduml
